@pale blue thoughts - I really love the details, but there are a lot more details to put for more understanding. But one thing, I didn't understand why you connected this with today's politics and religion. Channel seemed to have a bunch of knowledgeable and educated people, but you kept pronouncing names like "Rama", "Lakshmana". So, you're trying to make others understand that do not go for others porridge but you're trying to serve your own.

You mentioned in the video that in ancient times, there were hardly any written forms available, and so we all could understand the fact that when things are spreading verbally, they get changed like Chinese whispers. So, why don't you stick with the original one (Valmiki ji wrote) and try to decode it. If in Jain's belief, they have different versions of Ramayan, that doesn't mean it's false or just a story. The same goes with other authors and writers as well. I believe that the time and then society (of the writers) had a great impact as well as language barrier (translation from Sanskrit) in the writing and detailing.

This is the first time I watched your video. But the way you portrayed it with a cunning smile and vicious/derogative jokes, I was really waiting for the time when you connected this with the politics and a community's belief. That's what you did, your story telling has an agenda and if you're unable to see that if a story (as per your details) has such an inspirational power for thousands of years, then you have to go through the details once again.
